"Boudewijn Waijers" <kroisos@REMOVETHISWORD.home.nl> writes:

> If you really are sure there's nothing you can do, and you *are* going
> to die for certain, the thing to do is to #quit. Every character
> should think of his own interest first, and #quitting will raise your
> score by 10%.

I disagree vehemently.

The first consideration is that if you always quit when you are really
sure that you are going to die, you will never find out the tricks
that will let you survive those not-really-fatal-but-I-believe-so
situations.

Second, it is a misfeature that '#quit' lets you survive. If you are
in a situation where death REALLY is certain, then you REALLY should
die. The only way to escape the dungeon alive should be to climb the
level 1 stairs. There should not be a magic command to teleport you
out to safety while healing your fatal condition.

Third, the score is meaningless, especially if you use the viewpoint
of the character.


